WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
If you can't take the heat, get out of the molotov. That's right, it's time to talk about 1G.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.900
And you've probably seen this in Twitch chat when someone kills themselves with a molotov

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.880
in Counter-Strike.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.180
But, where did it come from?

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.640
Jaryd Lazar, also known as "Summit1G"

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.980
is one of CS:GO's most popular streamers,

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.840
but he's had stints on a number of teams in the past.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.480
One of those was as a stand-in for Splyce's Professor_Chaos at Dreamhack Austin 2016.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.320
Summit found himself in the spotlight after clutching out a round against Counter Logic Gaming's Fugly,

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.080
winning the game in the process.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.580
Only he didn't win the round because this happened.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.920
But no big deal right? Just take a round and win the map.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.660
Wrong.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.920
Wrong.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.320
Wrong.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.140
Wrong.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:39.380
Not only did Splyce drop that map 16-19 in overtime. They also lost Dust2 10-16

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.500
That meant they ultimately bombed out of Group A with an 0-2 record.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.240
Not exactly a great way to be remembered at a tournament.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:01.340
Ever since the embarrassing fail, whenever someone loses a 1v0 to a molotov

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.700
it's referred to as a Summit, or 1G for short.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:49.660
Summit, now finding humour in the incident, opened up on what it was like to be on the receiving end

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.560
of such an infamous blunder.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.520
Terrorists win.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:25.560
So there you have it, the next time your team's AWPer walks into their own molotov while their shins melt.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.800
You'll know exactly what to put in chat.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:33.940
Yo bruh, they have free donuts in the kitchen!

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.960
Donuts? Smokin!

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:39.820
Just look out for that blazing inferno in the hallway!

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.480
(Blazing Inferno)

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.520
1G!

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.080
Counter-Terrorists Win!

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.860
Molly makes you do strange things.

